# Fresh stack before browser MCP

When you are about to use a Playwright / browser MCP tool against the OpenAd web
app, confirm the local stack once at the start of the session. Do not restart
mid-session (Anvil is ephemeral; a restart wipes leases and sim state).

Windows (canonical):

```text
.\scripts\dev-up.cmd -Embed
.\scripts\sim-up.cmd
```

Then confirm:

- API `http://localhost:8000/v1/health` (port 8000)
- Web `http://localhost:5173` (port 5173)
- Embed demo `http://localhost:5174` when `-Embed` was used
- Anvil 8545, Postgres 15432
- Sim control `http://127.0.0.1:8610` after `sim-up`

Pause the sim tick loop (`sim_pause_loop` paused true) before interactive wallet
steps so MCP buys do not race sim nonces. Wear `?devwallet=pub-3` … `adv-9` only
(ADR-0013). Never Anvil `#0`–`#2`.

Never restart for pytest, vitest, `npm run typecheck`, or file-only edits.

If `GetDynamicTools` has no `playwright` namespace after `.cursor/mcp.json` lists
it, stop headed MCP and tell the user to enable the Playwright MCP server. Scripted
Playwright in `e2e/` may still run.
